From cf0c38d2ead14bdadb5ca9a7a968dc3d428a94a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhan Lou <zhan.lou@cixtech.com>
Date: Wed, 31 Dec 2025 17:07:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] DPTSW-22031: v4l2: enable deocde downscaling

When downscaling requirement is detected, try src pad caps negotiation
early before v4l2 output port is streamon, so that the downscaled
resolution can be sent to VPU firmware. VPU accepts downscale related
parameters at the very beginning only.

In this case, the 1st round of caps negotiation sets format for capture
port only but not configure other parameters,
gst_v4l2_object_set_format() must be called in the 2nd round of caps
negotiation which is after SOURCE_CHANGE event.

Signed-off-by: Zhan Lou <zhan.lou@cixtech.com>
Change-Id: I174c19c30aaa60c3527c7f70f5a6e93517af92fa

